  "reading": "Of 33 corruption cells, 11 are RNG-dependent and 22 are pure filters that never touch the generator; the second group is bit-identical across sessions (winner change rate 0.000) and is reported separately rather than averaged in, because including it dilutes the effect by construction. On the 11 RNG-dependent cells, scored with identical models and identical nominal seeds over 15 session pairs, the AUROC swing between sessions has median 0.0054 against a median winner margin of 0.0191. The winner changes at rate 0.079, and the swing exceeds the margin at rate 0.255. The ranking is therefore mostly stable: the defect corrupts the data in every affected cell, but only displaces the reported winner in the minority of cells where the top two methods are separated by less than the session noise. That minority is the part of a leaderboard a reader cannot trust."
